{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q019_stable_periodic_release_semantics","answer":"Verified from the current-release endpoint (/api/v1/releases/current, fetched 2026-10-13): the current stable release is SCOPe 2.08 (stable_label "2.08-stable", freeze date 2021-07-28, release date 2021-09-22, is_public true, is_comprehensive false, old_version null). The latest periodic update reported for it is version "2.08-2026-08-16", dated 2026-08-16.

Identifier to cite for reproducible work: the stable release selector "2.08" (label 2.08-stable), passed explicitly as the release in every release-scoped API call (e.g. /api/v1/releases/2.08/...). Stable releases are frozen, versioned snapshots whose SIDs, SUNIDs, SCCS strings, boundaries and lineages do not change, so an analysis pinned to 2.08 can be re-run and compared. Do not cite the bare word "current", because /releases/current will resolve to a different release once a new stable release is published.

What the periodic label means: "2.08-2026-08-16" is a dated incremental update layered on top of the 2.08 stable release. SCOPe periodic updates add newly released PDB entries that can be classified automatically (plus limited curation) without changing the existing 2.08 classification of previously classified domains; they are not a new comprehensive release (is_comprehensive is false for 2.08 itself) and they do not replace the stable release. The date in the label identifies which incremental snapshot was used. If an analysis depends on entries added only in a periodic update, cite the full periodic label (2.08-2026-08-16) together with the stable base (2.08) and the retrieval date, and note that the periodic layer may be superseded by later dated updates, whereas 2.08-stable will not change. Limit: the endpoint reports the labels and dates but does not itself describe the update policy; the semantics above follow the skill guidance that periodic updates do not replace stable releases.","evidence_used":["mcp__scope__get_scop_service_info","/api/v1/","/api/v1/releases/current","scop-homology/SKILL.md"]}]}
